  "summary": "Boat-horned matrilineal longhouses — spired gables, painted panels, and clan rooms of Minangkabau.",
  "description": "The rumah gadang shelters a Minangkabau clan's women under one soaring roof: multiple upswept gable horns (gonjong) rise like buffalo horns — memorializing the legendary buffalo victory that named the people — above a stilted longhouse of carved, painted panels. Each anjuang room belongs to a maternal line; ceremonies, marriages and council meals rotate through the spaces. Facades blaze with red, gold and black geometric carving, and the houses remain the ceremonial center of the world's largest matrilineal society.",
